sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch09-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "If descent with modification is true, periods at least as long as the whole time from the Silurian to the present must have passed before the lowest Silurian strata were laid down, and during them the world swarmed with living creatures.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Long ages of abundant life preceded the lowest Silurian strata";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter IX, “On the Imperfection of the Geological Record”; section “On their sudden appearance in the lowest known fossiliferous strata”. Scope: life on earth before the oldest then-known (Cambro-Silurian) fossiliferous strata"
}
